# Known Limitations

Freeing the Parrot 2.0 is an experimental interactive system.

The system consists of a client-facing Parrot interaction and a
post-session Silent Reader pipeline. Because the system is deployed
across a frontend and backend service, transient deployment or
runtime failures may occur.

## Session lifecycle

The intended flow is:

INPUT
→ LIVE CONVERSATION
→ I AM DONE
→ SESSION LOCK
→ POST-SESSION INTERPRETATION
→ READING DECK
→ PARTICIPANT SELECTION
→ MACHINE REVEAL
→ CONSENT / PURGE

If a failure occurs during post-session interpretation, refreshing
or restarting the session may be required.

## Data architecture

The Parrot does not receive Silent Reader telemetry during the
conversation.

Post-session analytical material is generated only after the
participant ends the interaction.

## Experimental status

This is an experimental research prototype rather than a
production-grade commercial system. Behaviour may vary depending
on the participant's interaction with the system.
